From 9b6d1546361ce4fef6a90568674a13463b68ef3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 06:50:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm/drm: CheckConnector() keeps what was read of
 the connector before

CheckConnector() (CDRMUtils::SetMode()) waits up to 7 s for a display that is not connected,
reading the connector again once a second. It replaced the read before with m_connector.reset(),
which freed the modes and the fields that Refresh() and Adopt() keep because they may still be
read: the selected mode of CDRMUtils is one of those modes, GetConnectorId() gives a pointer into
the read, and another thread may be reading it. And a read that failed (drmModeGetConnector() gave
nothing) left m_connector empty, which the next IsConnected() of the loop read through. It is
reachable where the connector in use was read again while nothing was connected to it.

It reads again with Refresh() now: what was read before is kept, a read that fails leaves the
connector as it was, and the values of its properties are read again with it, as Refresh() reads
them. Whether a display is connected is said as before.

Checked on the host with DRMConnector.cpp and DRMObject.cpp of the tree over a libdrm made of a
script, AddressSanitizer and UBSan: a display that comes back at the second read, one that never
does, reads that fail, and one connected from the start: 4 of 4; on the tree before, the three that
read again fail (a heap-use-after-free twice, a member access through a null pointer).
---
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMConnector.cpp | 8 ++++++--
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMConnector.h   | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMConnector.cpp b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMConnector.cpp
index b7f2344..5900a44 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMConnector.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMConnector.cpp
@@ -70,10 +70,14 @@ bool CDRMConnector::CheckConnector()
     retryCnt--;
     KODI::TIME::Sleep(1s);
 
-    m_connector.reset(drmModeGetConnector(m_fd, m_connector->connector_id));
+    // Hades: read again as Refresh() reads it: what was read before is kept (Adopt()), since what
+    // points into it may still read it (the selected mode of CDRMUtils is one of its modes), and a
+    // read that fails leaves the connector as it was. It used to be freed here, and m_connector left
+    // empty by a read that failed (the next IsConnected() read through no pointer).
+    Refresh();
   }
 
-  return m_connector->connection == DRM_MODE_CONNECTED;
+  return IsConnected();
 }
 
 bool CDRMConnector::Refresh()
diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMConnector.h b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMConnector.h
index 503fdb3..f6885bf 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMConnector.h
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMConnector.h
@@ -37,6 +37,8 @@ public:
   drmModeModeInfoPtr GetModeForIndex(int index) const { return &m_connector->modes[index]; }
 
   bool IsConnected() { return m_connector->connection == DRM_MODE_CONNECTED; }
+  //! Waits for a display that is not connected, 7 s at most, reading the connector again once a
+  //! second as Refresh() does (Hades: what was read before is kept); whether one is connected
   bool CheckConnector();
 
   std::vector<uint8_t> GetEDID() const;
-- 
